WEBVTT

00:16.683 --> 00:21.229
<i>I'll gather everyone who turned to stone!
You'll see!</i>

00:28.236 --> 00:30.405
<i>I'm sure someone has</i>

00:31.156 --> 00:33.533
<i>the Revival Fluid!</i>

00:36.578 --> 00:38.121
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA "JUMP COMICS"

02:29.232 --> 02:31.860
He found me!

02:41.161 --> 02:43.288
Please, don't frighten me like that.

02:45.832 --> 02:48.751
If Xeno's friends are here, that means...

03:10.648 --> 03:13.735
"That took you quite a while, Miss Suika."

03:15.069 --> 03:16.988
"I figured
something like this might happen,

03:17.071 --> 03:19.699
so I saved some Revival Fluid."

03:20.575 --> 03:23.661
"Now we can reunite with everyone!"

03:30.793 --> 03:33.880
That's not going to happen, is it?

03:40.637 --> 03:42.680
I feel so lonely!

03:42.764 --> 03:46.184
I want to see you all again soon!

03:49.562 --> 03:51.773
That hurt!

04:01.032 --> 04:03.076
If I let the broken part sit like this,

04:03.159 --> 04:05.870
it'll become impossible to fix.

04:08.248 --> 04:11.751
Maybe Senku has that medicine
to stick things together!

04:13.378 --> 04:15.672
Something's tucked away in his clothes.

04:18.174 --> 04:20.009
It's nothing but paper.

04:45.660 --> 04:46.661
Oh, right.

04:47.412 --> 04:49.247
Kohaku and the others were fighting.

04:49.330 --> 04:51.624
They could be chipped or broken too.

05:24.282 --> 05:27.493
If I could just ride a motorbike,

05:28.244 --> 05:32.498
<i>I could easily carry them
on those rolling tires.</i>

05:34.000 --> 05:36.335
Rolling tires...

05:37.503 --> 05:39.797
I think it was over here...

05:44.802 --> 05:46.554
Let's see...

06:14.082 --> 06:16.334
"You really worked hard, Suika!"

06:16.959 --> 06:21.005
"Once we're all together,
de-petrification will be a breeze."

06:21.672 --> 06:25.968
"You're really tired, aren't you?
Leave the rest to us and get some rest."

06:43.361 --> 06:46.489
No one's going to say anything like that.

06:48.616 --> 06:50.409
After all,

06:51.828 --> 06:53.746
I'm all alone in this world.

07:03.089 --> 07:04.882
<i>I've looked everywhere,</i>

07:04.966 --> 07:09.011
<i>but Luna and Chelsea
are nowhere to be found.</i>

07:09.095 --> 07:10.430
<i>But I'm pretty sure...</i>

07:11.347 --> 07:13.850
<i>they took over from me as revival agents</i>

07:13.933 --> 07:16.894
<i>and went off in the opposite direction.</i>

07:18.729 --> 07:20.231
I did it!

07:40.334 --> 07:43.671
Explorer Suika is ready to go!

07:46.632 --> 07:50.887
If we're revival agents,
they must have Revival Fluid on them.

07:59.645 --> 08:03.232
<i>They're the last two left,
and my last hope.</i>

08:29.008 --> 08:30.343
A vial?

08:36.349 --> 08:37.892
It fell and broke...

09:03.167 --> 09:05.461
Luna! Chelsea!

09:06.045 --> 09:07.713
I finally found you!

09:07.797 --> 09:10.424
It's all thanks to you
throwing down the Revival Fluid...

09:12.426 --> 09:14.053
<i>The Revival Fluid...</i>

09:17.473 --> 09:18.558
It's all gone...

09:18.641 --> 09:21.727
That was the last vial...

09:25.189 --> 09:29.193
<i>But I wouldn't have found them</i>

09:29.277 --> 09:33.072
<i>if it weren't for the Revival Fluid vial
they threw down...</i>

09:34.532 --> 09:36.492
This is new...

09:37.159 --> 09:39.704
Is it a map drawn by Chelsea?

09:42.164 --> 09:44.208
<i>So, this is it.</i>

09:45.126 --> 09:48.963
<i>No one's got any more Revival Fluid.</i>

09:53.593 --> 09:57.597
<i>I'll be all alone until the day I die...</i>

10:04.979 --> 10:08.566
<i>I wondered if I would bawl my eyes out
when I couldn't find Revival Fluid here,</i>

10:09.483 --> 10:12.486
<i>the place I thought was my last hope.</i>

10:19.702 --> 10:24.373
I'm not crying. I've grown up a little.

10:25.291 --> 10:27.960
I'm not a crybaby anymore.

10:47.605 --> 10:53.444
I'll think about what to do
once my stomach is full!

10:53.527 --> 10:56.113
First, let's go on an expedition
to find food!

10:57.782 --> 10:59.367
An expedition...

10:59.992 --> 11:01.202
<i>A map...</i>

11:27.395 --> 11:28.604
Even if you can't talk,

11:29.230 --> 11:32.733
I can still learn from you and do my best!

11:34.985 --> 11:39.448
<i>As time passes, it gets passed down...</i>

11:41.742 --> 11:44.745
<i>from one person to another...</i>

11:48.999 --> 11:50.292
Through papers and such...

11:51.419 --> 11:53.421
Wait... papers...

11:54.004 --> 11:55.923
It's nothing but paper.

12:00.553 --> 12:03.472
It's the recipe for the Revival Fluid!

12:04.849 --> 12:06.350
That's right.

12:06.976 --> 12:09.979
If there's none, I can make more.

12:11.522 --> 12:13.607
Because I'm a human.

12:14.733 --> 12:17.820
I'm going to meet them all again.

12:19.655 --> 12:21.574
We'll meet again!

12:24.452 --> 12:28.122
I just need to make science from scratch...

12:36.005 --> 12:40.759
It looks like... I'm a crybaby after all...

13:02.156 --> 13:03.908
Just like Senku...

13:05.868 --> 13:07.661
I'll do my best!

13:28.933 --> 13:31.143
Good morning, everyone!

13:42.821 --> 13:44.114
Let's see...

13:44.740 --> 13:49.161
Re-viv-al Flu-id...

13:49.245 --> 13:52.039
...Rec-i-pe...

13:53.332 --> 13:55.960
These character thingies are amazing.

13:56.043 --> 13:58.087
It's like having Senku talking

13:58.170 --> 14:00.381
about all his awesome science tricks!

14:00.965 --> 14:05.636
<i>I'm really glad I practiced
so I can read these characters.</i>

14:07.596 --> 14:08.556
But...

14:09.348 --> 14:14.061
reading them doesn't mean
I really understand!

14:14.144 --> 14:16.855
OSTWALD PROCESS

14:19.525 --> 14:23.404
The Revival Fluid's something...
nitric acid?

14:24.029 --> 14:29.034
There are one, two, three...
Three pages on how to make it.

14:32.830 --> 14:35.916
I think I'll skip this third page...

14:36.000 --> 14:39.336
The recipe on this
is going to take really long.

14:39.420 --> 14:41.797
And I want to meet everyone soon,

14:41.881 --> 14:44.174
so just the first two pages
should be fine, right?

14:44.925 --> 14:47.803
I'll tear the third paper and put it away.

14:51.432 --> 14:55.269
I'll do my best and try my first science!

14:56.061 --> 14:58.314
Even if I don't understand at all,

14:58.397 --> 15:01.358
if I just follow what's written,
I'll be able to do it!

15:44.401 --> 15:48.697
Senku and the others worked so hard
every day with things like this.

15:49.281 --> 15:53.452
There's no way I could do
something this hard all of a sudden!

15:53.535 --> 15:56.664
I guess I'm not useful after all...

16:08.676 --> 16:12.638
The third page I put away
might take a long time,

16:13.889 --> 16:16.684
but I guess I have to follow it!

16:24.024 --> 16:26.235
POO

16:56.265 --> 16:59.685
It stinks!

17:03.605 --> 17:06.316
These are not enough...

17:07.693 --> 17:09.737
Other than that...

17:10.821 --> 17:12.614
<i>I could use my own poo!</i>

17:14.033 --> 17:18.495
No! I don't want to!

17:31.091 --> 17:33.469
GUANO
WATERFOWL ISLAND

17:50.944 --> 17:55.115
All the white stuff on this island
is bird poo!

17:59.828 --> 18:01.997
NITRIC ACID FIELD

18:08.045 --> 18:11.173
"After putting the poop
with the plant ashes,

18:11.256 --> 18:14.301
it has to stay buried for almost a year..."

18:14.384 --> 18:17.846
A year? That's too long!

18:20.432 --> 18:24.812
After that, I have to cook some shells...

18:24.895 --> 18:27.064
REACTION
DISOLVES IN WATER

18:28.690 --> 18:32.194
I don't really know
what I'm doing anymore, so...

18:32.277 --> 18:36.031
That's it! I can just make one of those.

18:38.826 --> 18:42.287
The thing that Senku and Chrome
used to write down!

18:50.087 --> 18:53.382
START
STRAW, WATER, SHELL

18:55.050 --> 18:59.012
FIRE, POO, ALCOHOL, NITRIC ACID STONE
SULFURIC ACID, REVIVAL FLUID

19:02.599 --> 19:05.185
NITRIC ACID FIELD

19:05.936 --> 19:08.063
I have to be careful not to put in

19:08.147 --> 19:11.108
too much or too little water
in the saltpeter field.

20:27.517 --> 20:30.562
<i>I'll keep trying again and again!</i>

21:01.301 --> 21:02.302
<i>Even if it takes a year,</i>

21:03.512 --> 21:05.055
<i>or I get it wrong again...</i>

21:10.852 --> 21:12.229
<i>Again...</i>

21:26.326 --> 21:27.744
<i>And again...</i>

21:50.142 --> 21:51.435
<i>And again...</i>

21:57.399 --> 21:59.234
<i>And again, and again...</i>

22:02.863 --> 22:04.156
<i>And again...!</i>

22:05.907 --> 22:07.284
<i>And again...!</i>

22:08.910 --> 22:10.287
<i>And again!</i>

22:20.672 --> 22:24.593
<i>...seven, eight, nine...</i>

22:53.246 --> 22:56.750
Sorry for making you wait this long...

22:59.628 --> 23:02.964
I guess you don't recognize me anymore...

23:07.469 --> 23:10.055
You truly are helpful...

23:22.275 --> 23:23.902
Suika.

23:36.581 --> 23:38.875
Roughly seven years...

23:41.253 --> 23:42.838
You were really fast.

23:53.223 --> 23:55.892
NEXT EPISODE

23:55.976 --> 23:57.978
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:58.061 --> 23:59.938
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM
MAY BE DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL,

24:00.021 --> 24:00.897
SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:00.981 --> 24:01.940
